so it looks like uh it's happening guys  um i got some breaking news that's why  this video is gonna be a little bit less  edited and structured than usual but  this is uh something that just came out  a while ago and i do think we have to  talk about it one piece apparently is  preparing for the final saga slash final  arc  what the hell  seriously um so in case you don't know  what's happening we got a post from the  official one piece twitter account in  japanese where we basically got a  handwritten message by ichiro oda the  author of one piece and in this message  he talks about a bunch of things but the  core thing is one piece is gonna be on  break for about four weeks so about a  month which is gonna be like four  chapters in a row basically which is  relatively rare oda sensei as you might  know takes his breaks but never in that  sort of scale it's something quite new  that we're not used to and so he gives  us a bunch of explanations for why this  is happening this is going to be in july  quite soon so we're going to get like  one or two more chapters and then the  breaks gonna happen there's a bunch of  things he throws into that post let's  let's i would say let's start actually  with the most important part oda wants  to take a break in part apparently  because he wants to take the time to  prepare the story and prepare his  thoughts for the final of the story and  preparing to finish and wrap up one  piece which let's be real is  huge i mean we're talking about the  series ending that has been going on for  over 20 years it's something that has  been hinted at and oda has mentioned  over and over and over again that he  will want to end this at some point in  the next five years and it always kept  pushing forward and right now honestly  with wano and everything that's going on  it doesn't really feel like we're super  close to the ending but once again this  seems to be proof that we're actually  closer to the end than we all might  think which  man called sandman on twitter who  translates a lot of the shonen jump and  one piece related news from japanese is  it once again people on twitter keep  saying it's the final arc and after wano  the final arc is gonna happen but to be  fair this post isn't quite as obvious  but it does indeed say that oda kind of  phrases is as he wants to revise the  story  so he can start wrapping up the final  arc or final saga it's kind of a bit  ambiguous here which he means though  let's be real it can't be a final arc  because even if we skipped elbaf which  is unlikely it would be left tail and  the final war which is already two arcs  so i personally would say it's  definitely talking about the final saga  which would include a bunch of arcs that  together kind of form the endgame of one  piece and so basically his argument is  that he wants to revise the story in  other words collect his thoughts and  structure everything out in a proper way  so he can start wrapping up the story  now it sounds like and people on twitter  obviously make it sound like one piece  is about to end very soon it's wano  we're wrapping up one or right away um  before this break still and then we're  gonna head right into the last arc find  the one piece one piece over clearly  this is not what this is about it's  definitely going into a direction where  one piece or oda and the team in general  want to move things along to push one  piece towards the ending but it says  nothing about you know rushing there or  that it's gonna be right away so it says  neither that wano is gonna end right  away before this break which is very  unrealistic i think or even if it might  happen it will take a while until we  actually leave wano and wrap everything  up there and then secondly it also  doesn't mean that right after this break  we go into like the final arc in the  final saga right away so i think what it  really says is it's a summer break oda  wants to collect his thoughts write his  notes structure the story and prepare  everything in calm without having to  worry about writing a manga in the  meantime and then basically prepare for  the upcoming arcs that like as a package  together form the final big saga of the  story which i would personally assume is  elbaf love tale maybe roadstar who knows  and then the final war however that will  take place in whatever shape or form  another reason for the break which i  think is important to mention because  the only reason isn't only that oda  wants to sit down take a break now and  then you know write and like plan  everything out for the final season but  it's also because he is involved in the  netflix series where he originally  wanted to travel to africa to visit the  filming which was got cancelled because  of covet but it still played into that  that he originally wanted to take that  time off um that didn't happen and the  second thing is that he's also directing  film red which is scheduled in july i  want to say to come out here in japan  which is two major project where he's  directly involved and where he basically  wanted to take time off to take care of  those projects as well because the man  already sleeps little enough i don't  think we have to have him sleep even  less while like writing the story so the  film movie red coming out soon and  netflix series he's involved in both of  them so directly that he just needed to  take a big break to still work basically  and make sure those projects um are  coming to a conclusion or shaping the  way that he envisions them to be so it's  these three reasons gathering his  thoughts a movie and the netflix tv show  which is why he takes a break i still  think it's giant news but i think also  at the same time we should all not  overreact it's a lot more vague in the  japanese version i think personally than  people make it seem on twitter so it  does theme in conclusion it does seem  like we're moving towards the final arc  in one piece it's about to happen i do  think sounds apparently like wano is  about to wrap up relatively soon not  necessarily in the next few chapters but  soon and then we're gonna move into the  final saga which is gonna consist of  multiple arcs most likely so we're still  years away from one piece ending in case  you're worried about that or in case you  wanted it to rub out very soon i don't  think that's gonna happen but  nonetheless i think um we're probably  talking less than ten years so maybe the  five-year timeline that oda has  originally scheduled out last year or  was it two years ago already i think  that is getting more and more likely so  we're definitely in the end game now but  nonetheless since we're talking about  scheduling everything out i do think  it's all gonna take its time there's so  many things to wrap up so many places we  still have to visit so many enemies  still to face i think we're good for a  while with content and honestly i'm  really excited to move onwards to the  end game meet shanks meet blackbeard  find the one piece and hopefully take  down the world government so yeah thanks  for tuning in for this quick update if  you want something to watch next i  strongly recommend you check out my  review of yamato joining the crew here
 

